# .dockerignore — what does NOT get COPYed into the backend / cli image.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Load-bearing for two reasons:
#
#   1. PRIVACY.  Without this file, `docker build .` would slurp `data/`,
#      `outputs/`, `tmp/`, `chroma_db/`, and `.env` into the image. The
#      first four contain real client RFI text; .env contains the
#      Mistral API key. None of those belong in a built image.
#
#   2. IMAGE SIZE.  The ChromaDB store + outputs/ + frontend/node_modules
#      together are tens of MB the runtime doesn't need.
#
# Mirror of .gitignore plus a few extras that ARE git-committed but
# shouldn't be in the image (e.g. docs/, frontend/ when building the
# backend image).

# --- Privacy-critical (matches .gitignore) -------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.key
data/*.xlsx
data/*.xls
data/*.csv
data/*.pdf
data/*.docx
config_rfi_*.json
outputs/
chroma_db/
*.sqlite3
tmp/

# --- The frontend lives in its own image; don't bake it into the backend
frontend/

# --- Build / source-control noise ----------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.github/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Editor / OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude/

# --- Docs / tooling not needed at runtime --------------------------------
docs/
*.md
!README.md
